WEBVTT

00:03.920 --> 00:04.280
All right.

00:04.280 --> 00:06.400
So with that you have understood what is CTE.

00:06.680 --> 00:10.000
Now the question is why do we need CTE in the first place?

00:10.120 --> 00:12.400
What is the main purpose of the CTE?

00:12.640 --> 00:14.040
Let's go back to the sketch.

00:14.080 --> 00:18.120
Now let's say in our complex SQL task we have to do the following step.

00:18.160 --> 00:23.440
Step one we have to go and join the tables together in order to prepare all the data that we need for

00:23.440 --> 00:24.200
the next step.

00:24.200 --> 00:26.960
And now in the second step, we have to go and aggregate the data.

00:27.000 --> 00:28.840
Maybe we are doing summarizations.

00:28.880 --> 00:34.280
Now in our task we have to do as well different types of aggregations based on different data.

00:34.280 --> 00:39.320
And now what might happen is that we have to go and join again the same tables in order to prepare the

00:39.320 --> 00:44.960
data and perform different type of aggregations, like for example, the average, which can be in the

00:44.960 --> 00:45.800
last step.

00:45.840 --> 00:50.680
Now we have learned before we can go and use the subqueries in order to make this logical flow.

00:50.760 --> 00:54.320
So for step one, step two, step three, we will have subqueries.

00:54.320 --> 00:57.320
And the final step is going to be in the main query.

00:57.320 --> 01:02.920
But now if we keep doing this we're going to have a problem, and that is we are repeating the same

01:02.920 --> 01:04.520
step more than once.

01:04.520 --> 01:09.920
So we are joining the table twice in step number one and three for different purposes, which cause

01:09.920 --> 01:12.760
us to have two different subqueries.

01:12.760 --> 01:14.320
That looks exactly the same.

01:14.320 --> 01:17.280
And this is exactly the weak point of the subqueries.

01:17.440 --> 01:20.080
It might introduce redundancies.

01:20.080 --> 01:25.960
So that means the subqueries alone will not help you to eliminate all the duplicates in your code.

01:26.000 --> 01:29.240
But still we have different techniques in order to solve this issue.

01:29.240 --> 01:34.000
So what we're going to do, we're going to have only one step in order to join the tables.

01:34.000 --> 01:37.960
And then this data can be used in the step two in order to aggregate the data.

01:37.960 --> 01:41.560
And then we don't need the step three of joining again the data.

01:41.560 --> 01:43.960
We can reuse the step one.

01:43.960 --> 01:49.720
And we're going to use the same data for the step four which is aggregating the data using average.

01:49.720 --> 01:53.080
And we can do this with the help of the amazing CTE.

01:53.120 --> 01:57.800
So now if we compare the steps in the subqueries with the steps with the CTE, you can see with the

01:57.800 --> 02:04.070
CTE we are reducing the number of steps which can lead to reduce the size of the query.

02:04.070 --> 02:08.510
So now again here in subquery we think about the steps from bottom to top.

02:08.510 --> 02:12.390
But in the CTE it's the way around we think from top to bottom.

02:12.390 --> 02:15.590
So that means the first step on the top is going to be joining the tables.

02:15.590 --> 02:17.950
And then below it's going to be step two and step three.

02:17.990 --> 02:21.390
And of course since we are repeating the join we are going to put it in CTE.

02:21.430 --> 02:25.750
And then we can use it twice in different places in the main query.

02:25.750 --> 02:28.270
So as you can see there are a lot of benefits of the CTE.

02:28.510 --> 02:29.710
It's like the subqueries.

02:29.710 --> 02:36.830
We are breaking down complex queries into smaller pieces that are easier to write, manage, understand

02:36.830 --> 02:41.950
and as well we have like a logical flow from step one, two, three, but with one more benefit.

02:41.990 --> 02:47.630
Thus we reduce the redundancies of our code so we don't have to join the tables twice.

02:47.630 --> 02:51.750
Now I'm going to show you a simple example how the CTE makes our life easier.

02:51.750 --> 02:54.230
In our query, we might have to do different stuff.

02:54.230 --> 02:57.790
Like for example, we have to go and find the top customers.

02:57.790 --> 03:03.430
So we can put this in one CTE and we might need as well to calculate what are the top products.

03:03.430 --> 03:06.190
And we can put as well this in another city.

03:06.230 --> 03:08.630
So you don't have to put everything in one big city.

03:08.670 --> 03:11.350
Then you're going to have the same issue of having complex query.

03:11.390 --> 03:15.430
And let's say that we have as well to find and calculate the daily revenue.

03:15.470 --> 03:17.790
And for this as well, we have to put it in one city.

03:17.830 --> 03:22.870
Now, once we have all those parts, we can put everything together in the main query.

03:22.870 --> 03:27.790
So now if we look to this structure you can see it's really easy to understand this code.

03:27.790 --> 03:28.950
It's easy to read.

03:28.950 --> 03:32.630
So CTE improves the readability of our queries.

03:32.630 --> 03:38.790
So that means your code is divided into clear sections making it easier to understand what each part

03:38.830 --> 03:39.310
does.

03:39.350 --> 03:45.270
Now if you keep looking to this we have another advantage of the CTE introduces modularity.

03:45.270 --> 03:49.870
So that means it breaks your code into smaller manageable parts.

03:49.870 --> 03:56.940
So this means instead of writing one huge complex query, you break it down into smaller chunks using

03:56.980 --> 03:57.380
CTE.

03:57.540 --> 04:03.540
Each CTE is like self-contained and handles specific part of the problem, and then you can combine

04:03.540 --> 04:05.460
them all together in the final query.

04:05.500 --> 04:09.060
It's like we are putting together a puzzle piece by piece.

04:09.100 --> 04:13.260
And now one very important advantage of the CTE is the reusability.

04:13.260 --> 04:18.420
So that means we can have a result set that is used multiple times inside our query.

04:18.420 --> 04:23.660
So that means you write the logic the code only once and then use it in different places inside your

04:23.660 --> 04:24.180
query.

04:24.180 --> 04:25.180
This is very important.

04:25.220 --> 04:30.700
Not only you are wasting time writing the same stuff over and over, but also it reduces the errors

04:30.700 --> 04:35.380
and mistakes that you might do if you are repeating the same code, especially if later you want to

04:35.380 --> 04:40.780
go and change the logic, then you have to go and visit each time you have done this logic, and then

04:40.820 --> 04:43.540
do the changes and you might forget some places.

04:43.540 --> 04:45.460
That's why the city is amazing.

04:45.460 --> 04:49.980
You can write the logic once and then you go and reuse it in different places.

04:49.980 --> 04:55.260
So these are the advantages of using this technique, the CTE inside your queries.
